# Evaluation No 2 and Remediation No 2 (Week 10)

> ASSESS:
  **Evaluation No 2 (2 periods).** Covers Lessons 17–34: network equipment; setting up a P2P network; selecting equipment and designing a network; intranet/extranet; VPNs and privacy protocols; computer and network security; data protection and access control; validation and verification; transmission modes and CSMA/CD–CA; broadband/narrowband; serial/parallel, synchronous/asynchronous, analog/digital; guided/unguided media; peripheral control mechanisms; protocols and TCP/IP; protocol suites and the OSI model.
  **Suggested structure (60 marks):** Part A – 15 MCQ/short items (15 marks); Part B – structured questions (30 marks), e.g. (i) identify components from a diagram, differentiate hub/switch/router, list equipment for a two-block school with factors; (ii) design intranet/extranet/VPN for a described organisation, explain digital signatures and the firewall rules for the VPN; (iii) CIA threat table and access-control plan with RBAC and encryption; (iv) validation rules and verification methods for a given form; (v) classify scenarios by transmission mode, access method, bandwidth class and transmission type; choose media for three contexts with criteria; (vi) determine peripheral-control techniques in scenarios; (vii) map twelve protocols to OSI layers and explain TCP reliability; Part C – **practical (15 marks)**: set up sharing between two PCs and verify with ping/share access; configure Data Validation and double entry in a spreadsheet; set folder permissions for a group; (optional) capture and identify a TCP handshake or connect a VPN client.
  **Remediation No 2 (1–2 periods).** From item analysis: (1) equipment/design – station rotation and design canvas rework; (2) security block – "fix the breach" case with encryption/permissions redo on the lab server; (3) transmission – card sorts and waveform drawing clinic; (4) protocols/OSI – human-stack relay and mapping wall; (5) peer tutoring and a short re-test on the weakest objectives for under-performing learners before Lesson 35.

